scripts.features:
Revamped!
Anti Loggers via Webhooks {
Prevents unauthorized logging attempts by detecting and blocking webhook-based data transfers.
}
Anti Robux Stealers {
Protects against malicious attempts to steal robux by denying Prompt, Perform purchase requests.
}
Military Grade Protection {
 Offers amazing security, No script can ever steal your information without you allowing it to.
}
Anti HWID Stealing {
 Blocks attempts to steal HWID (Hardware ID) information, which hackers can 
 use to get you banned on different games such as roblox, fortnite, etc.
}
Anti Chat Ban {
 Blocks attempt to force your user to chat inappropriate/things you didn't ask to 
 chat, Which could be used to get you banned.
}
Anti Unallowed HTTP Post Requests {
 Blocks HTTP Post requests that are not allowed by you, These requests will only 
 work after you have clicked allowed and won't instantly work when you click 
 allow.
}
Notifies When Get Requests Are Used {
 Notifies you in the tabs list whenever a get request is used, You can use this for 
 your own scripts too!
}
Source Code Copy {
 Lets you copy the source code of POST requests, Source code is how the script was written
}
"What can I do with this?"
Well, First let's talk about webhooks.
Say you don't wanna get logged or get your data sent to a webhook, While using this if a post request is sent you can view it and copy it as a lua table, Then run it through a webhook spammer and spam the webhook!
Or you can delete it,
Second, You can execute almost ANY script without having to worry about being logged, hacked or scammed.
Third, Bypass whitelist systems that use http requests to check if hardware ids are in a pastebin, list etc.
Many more features!
Beats Protectio & Guardian v2
v1.0.1 (The Requests Update) {
 Fixed GET requests returning an error
 New features {
  Copy As {
   cURL,
   Source,
   Python coming soon
  },
  HeadersViewer {
   Allows you to view headers in requests that you weren't able to see before
  },
  More GET detection {
   Script now also detects game.HttpGet, game.HttpGetAsync, game:HttpGet, request(), etc...
  }
 },
 Script now shows what the request was requested with (eg: http.request, request, game.HttpGet),
 Script now returns Cookies and Headers from GET or POST requests to third 
 party websites to avoid detection & not break scripts.
 Known Bugs:
 Requests may duplicate or create 2 tabs instead of one.
}

